    "id": "p51-q17-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$(A\\cap B)\\cup(\\overline A\\cap B)=A$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "False. The left side equals $B$.",
      "worked": "False. The two intersections contain the elements of $B$ inside $A$ and outside $A$. Their union is therefore $B$, which need not equal $A$. For example, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$ in $U=\\{1,2\\}$ give a left side of $\\{2\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
